    "text": "The energy of a system as a function of time <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> is given as <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> , where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The measurement of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> has an error of 1.25%. If the error in the measurement of time is 1.50%, the percentage error in the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> s is\r\r<div id=\"gtx-trans\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 17px; top: 74px;\">\r<div class=\"gtx-trans-icon\">&nbsp;</div>\r</div>\r"
